 (Zero Flag)","C":"SF (Sign Flag)","D":"OF (Overflow Flag)"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0021","type":"mcq","stem":"Which flag indicates a borrow occurred in subtraction?","options":{"A":"ZF","B":"CF","C":"OF","D":"PF"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0022","type":"mcq","stem":"Which flag indicates signed overflow?","options":{"A":"CF","B":"OF","C":"ZF","D":"AF"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0023","type":"mcq","stem":"Which flag indicates the sign of the result (bit 15)?","options":{"A":"CF","B":"ZF","C":"SF","D":"PF"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0024","type":"mcq","stem":"The Auxiliary Carry Flag (AF) is used for:","options":{"A":"Signed arithmetic","B":"BCD arithmetic","C":"Floating-point","D":"String operations"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0025","type":"mcq","stem":"The Parity Flag (PF) is set when:","options":{"A":"Result is even","B":"Result has even number of 1s","C":"Result is positive","D":"Result is odd"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0026","type":"mcq","stem":"The Trap Flag (TF) is used for:","options":{"A":"Interrupt handling","B":"Single-stepping (debugging)","C":"String operations","D":"Direction control"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0027","type":"mcq","stem":"The Interrupt Flag (IF) controls:","options":{"A":"Hardware interrupts (INTR)","B":"Software interrupts","C":"Exceptions","D":"All interrupts"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0028","type":"mcq","stem":"The Direction Flag (DF) affects which instructions?","options":{"A":"Arithmetic","B":"String instructions (MOVS, STOS, etc.)","C":"Jump instructions","D":"Stack operations"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0029","type":"mcq","stem":"How many interrupt types can the 8086 handle?","options":{"A":"128","B":"256","C":"512","D":"1024"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0030","type":"mcq","stem":"The Interrupt Vector Table (IVT) is located at:","options":{"A":"0000:0000","B":"FFFF:0000","C":"0000:FFFF","D":"F000:0000"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0