","options":{"A":"AX","B":"BX","C":"CX","D":"DX"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0052","type":"mcq","stem":"In MUL instruction, the result of multiplying AX by a 16-bit operand is stored in:","options":{"A":"AX only","B":"DX:AX","C":"CX:BX","D":"BX:AX"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0053","type":"mcq","stem":"In DIV instruction, dividing DX:AX by a 16-bit operand stores the quotient in:","options":{"A":"DX","B":"AX","C":"BX","D":"CX"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0054","type":"mcq","stem":"Which register pair is used for 32-bit multiplication result?","options":{"A":"BX:CX","B":"DX:AX","C":"DS:SI","D":"CS:IP"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0055","type":"mcq","stem":"The CL register is used as the count in which instructions?","options":{"A":"LOOP and REP","B":"SHL, SHR, ROL, ROR","C":"MOV and XCHG","D":"PUSH and POP"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0056","type":"mcq","stem":"What is the size of each general-purpose register (AX, BX, CX, DX) in the 8086?","options":{"A":"8 bits","B":"16 bits","C":"32 bits","D":"64 bits"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0057","type":"mcq","stem":"Which registers can be split into high and low 8-bit parts?","options":{"A":"SI and DI","B":"AX, BX, CX, DX","C":"SP and BP","D":"CS and DS"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0058","type":"mcq","stem":"Which register cannot be used as a memory pointer in the 8086?","options":{"A":"BX","B":"BP","C":"SI","D":"CX"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0059","type":"mcq","stem":"When using [BP] as a memory pointer, the default segment is:","options":{"A":"DS","B":"SS","C":"CS","D":"ES"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0060","type":"mcq","stem":"When using [BX] as a memory pointer, the default segment is:","options":{"A":"DS","B":"SS","C":"CS","D":"ES"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0061","type":"mcq","stem":"The segment override prefix allows you to:","options":{"A":"Change the default segment for one instruction","B":"Disable interrupts","C":"Switch to protected mode","D":"Change the clock speed"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0062","type":"mcq","stem":"Which register is used for I/O port addressing when the port number > 255?","options":{"A":"AX","B":"BX","C":"DX","D":"CX"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0063","type":"mcq","stem":"The MOV instruction can transfer data between:","options":{"A":"Register to register only","B":"Memory to register and vice versa","C":"Immediate to register/memory","D":"All of the above"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0064","type":"mcq","stem":"Which instruction cannot move data directly from memory to memory?","options":{"A":"MOV","B":"PUSH","C":"POP","D":"XCHG"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0065","type":"mcq","stem":"The XCHG instruction swaps the contents of:","options":{"A":"Two registers","B":"A register and memory","C":"Both A and B","D":"Two memory locations"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0066","type":"mcq","stem":"The LEA instruction is used to:","options":{"A":"Load data from memory","B":"Load the effective address (offset) into a register","C":"Load a segment register","D":"Load the flags"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0067","type":"mcq","stem":"LEA BX, [SI+5] is equivalent to:","options":{"A":"MOV BX, [SI+5]","B":"MOV BX, SI","C":"MOV BX, SI; ADD BX, 5","D":"ADD BX, SI, 5"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0068","type":"mcq","stem":"The PUSH instruction does what to SP?","options":{"A":"Increments SP by 2","B":"Decrements SP by 2","C":"Does not change SP","D":"Sets SP to 0"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0069","type":"mcq","stem":"The POP instruction does what to SP?","options":{"A":"Decrements SP by 2","B":"Increments SP by 2","C":"Sets SP to 0","D":"Does not change SP"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0070","type":"mcq","stem":"How many addressing modes does the 8086 support?","options":{"A":"4","B":"6","C":"8","D":"12"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0071","type":"mcq","stem":"In immediate addressing, the operand is:","options":{"A":