"A":"BX + 6, relative to SS","B":"BX + 6, relative to DS","C":"BX + 6, relative to CS","D":"BX + 6, relative to ES"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0090","type":"mcq","stem":"To override the default segment for [BX], you would use:","options":{"A":"ES: [BX]","B":"CS: [BX]","C":"SS: [BX]","D":"Any of the above"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0091","type":"mcq","stem":"Which is NOT a valid 8086 addressing mode combination?","options":{"A":"[BX+SI]","B":"[AX+BX]","C":"[BP+DI]","D":"[BX+DI+10]"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0092","type":"mcq","stem":"The physical address for CS:IP = 1000:2000 is:","options":{"A":"3000h","B":"12000h","C":"10000h","D":"22000h"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0093","type":"mcq","stem":"If DS = 2000h and BX = 0100h, the physical address of [BX] is:","options":{"A":"2010h","B":"20100h","C":"21000h","D":"20001h"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0094","type":"mcq","stem":"Two different segment:offset pairs can point to the same physical address. This is called:","options":{"A":"Address aliasing","B":"Segment overlap","C":"Address wrapping","D":"Logical address equivalence"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0095","type":"mcq","stem":"The ADD instruction affects which flags?","options":{"A":"CF, ZF, SF, OF, AF, PF","B":"Only CF and ZF","C":"Only IF and TF","D":"No flags"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0096","type":"mcq","stem":"The SUB instruction affects which flags?","options":{"A":"Same as ADD","B":"Only CF and ZF","C":"Only SF and OF","D":"No flags"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0097","type":"mcq","stem":"The INC instruction affects which flags?","options":{"A":"All flags including CF","B":"All flags except CF","C":"Only ZF and SF","D":"No flags"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0098","type":"mcq","stem":"The DEC instruction affects which flags?","options":{"A":"All flags including CF","B":"All flags except CF","C":"Only ZF","D":"No flags"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0099","type":"mcq","stem":"The CMP instruction does what?","options":{"A":"Adds two operands","B":"Subtracts operands and sets flags but discards result","C":"Multiplies operands","D":"Swaps operands"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0100","type":"mcq","stem":"After CMP AX, BX, if ZF=1, it means:","options":{"A":"AX > BX","B":"AX < BX","C":"AX = BX","D":"AX and BX are both zero"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0101","type":"mcq","stem":"After CMP AX, BX, if CF=1 (unsigned), it means:","options":{"A":"AX > BX","B":"AX < BX","C":"AX = BX","D":"Overflow occurred"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0102","type":"mcq","stem":"The JMP instruction is:","options":{"A":"Conditional","B":"Unconditional","C":"Both","D":"Neither"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0103","type":"mcq","stem":"How many conditional jump instructions does the 8086 have?","options":{"A":"8","B":"16","C":"18","D":"24"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0104","type":"mcq","stem":"JE (Jump if Equal) is the same as:","options":{"A":"JZ","B":"JNE","C":"JG","D":"JL"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0105","type":"mcq","stem":"JNE (Jump if Not Equal) is the same as:","options":{"A":"JZ","B":"JNZ","C":"JC","D":"JNC"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0106","type":"mcq","stem":"JA (Jump if Above) checks which flags (unsigned)?","options":{"A":"CF=0 and ZF=0","B":"CF=1","C":"ZF=1","D":"SF≠OF"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0107","type":"mcq","stem":"JG (Jump if Greater) checks which flags (signed)?","options":{"A":"ZF=0 and SF=OF","B":"CF=0","C":"ZF=1","D":"SF≠OF"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0108","type":"mcq","stem":"The LOOP instruction does what?","options":{"A":"Decrements CX and jumps if CX≠0","B":"Increments CX and jumps","C":"Jumps unconditionally","D":"Does not affect CX"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0109","type":"mcq","stem":"LOOPE (Loop if Equal) decrements CX and jumps if:","options":{"A":"CX≠0 only","B":"CX≠0 and ZF=1","C":"CX≠0 and ZF=0","D":"ZF=1 only"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0110","type":"mcq","stem":"LOOPNE (Loop if Not Equal) decrements CX and jumps if:","options":{"A":"CX≠0 only","B":"CX≠0 and ZF=1","C":"CX≠0 and ZF=0","D":"ZF=0 only"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0111","type":"mcq","stem":"The MUL instruction performs ___ multiplication.","options":{"A":"Signed","B":"Unsigned","C":"Both","D":"Floating-point"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0112","type":"mcq","stem":"The IMUL instruction performs ___ multiplication.","options":{"A":"Signed","B":"Unsigned","C":"Both","D":"Floating-point"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0113","type":"mcq","stem":"MUL BL multiplies AL by BL and stores the result in:","options":{"A":"AL","B":"AX","C":"DX:AX","D":"BL"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0114","type":"mcq","stem":"MUL BX multiplies AX by BX and stores the result in:","options":{"A":"AX","B":"BX","C":"DX:AX","D":"CX:BX"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0115","type":"mcq","stem":"DIV BL divides AX by BL and stores the quotient in:","options":{"A":"AL","B":"AH","C":"AX","D":"BL"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0116","type":"mcq","stem":"DIV BX divides DX:AX by BX and stores the quotient in:","options":{"A":"AX (quotient), DX (remainder)","B":"DX (quotient), AX (remainder)","C":"BX (quotient), CX (remainder)","D":"AX only"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0117","type":"mcq","stem":"The CBW instruction does what?","options":{"A":"Converts byte to word (sign-extends AL to AX)","B":"Converts word to byte","C":"Clears AX","D":"Swaps AH and AL"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0118","type":"mcq","stem":"The CWD instruction does what?","options":{"A":"Converts word to doubleword (sign-extends AX to DX:AX)","B":"Converts doubleword to word","C":"Clears DX","D":"Swaps AX and DX"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-futa-fsen102-0119","type":"mcq","stem":"The NEG instruction does what?","options":{"A":"Makes the operand zero","B":"Computes two's complement (0 - operand)","C":"Sets all bits to 1","D":"Reverses bit order"},"marks":1},{"id":"uni-